    history_html: `<p><strong>2021:</strong> Battlefield 2042 launched with significant live-service integration, featuring a premium cosmetic shop alongside its battle pass system. Initial monetization was aggressive compared to previous entries.</p><p><strong>2022:</strong> Post-launch updates introduced seasonal cosmetics with increasingly higher price points. The game faced criticism for high cosmetic costs relative to cosmetic quality during its early rough period.</p><p><strong>2023:</strong> Significant pivot toward cosmetic quality improvements. Limited-time seasonal cosmetics became the primary focus, with cross-event cosmetic returns maintaining cosmetic relevance across seasons.</p><p><strong>2024:</strong> Battlefield 2042 settled into a stable live-service model with consistent seasonal cosmetic releases. The shop pricing stabilized around $10-20 per premium cosmetic bundle.</p>`,
