    editorial_html: `<p>Battlefield 2042's cosmetic shop represents the increasingly aggressive monetization of AAA multiplayer shooters. While the cosmetics themselves don't impact gameplay directly, the psychological pressure created by limited-time availability and seasonal exclusivity pushes players toward spending patterns more reminiscent of gacha games than traditional cosmetic stores.</p><p>The pricing sits in the middle ground—more expensive than fair-value games like Splatoon 3 but justified by the cosmetics' visual quality and the game's AAA production budget. However, the constant rotation of limited items and seasonal passes encourages ongoing spending rather than one-time cosmetic purchases.</p><p>For players comfortable with live-service spending models, Battlefield 2042's cosmetics offer decent variety and quality. For those seeking value, waiting for seasonal sales or focusing on free cosmetics is advisable.</p>`
