    overview_html: `<p><strong>Splatoon 3</strong> represents one of the fairest cosmetic monetization models in gaming. All cosmetics can be purchased using Super Sea Snails, earnable entirely for free through regular gameplay. The cosmetic shop rotates gear seasonally, offering hats, clothing, and shoes that affect both aesthetics and gameplay abilities equally.</p><p>Nintendo's approach prioritizes player choice and accessibility. Cosmetics are never time-limited or exclusive; everything eventually rotates back into the shop. This eliminates FOMO and allows players to build their cosmetic collection at their own pace without spending money.</p>`,
    pity_explanation_html: `<p>Splatoon 3 has no pity system because it has no randomization or gacha mechanics. All cosmetics are available for direct purchase at consistent prices, making pity systems unnecessary. Players know exactly what they're buying and the cost in advance.</p>`,
    history_html: `<p><strong>2022:</strong> Splatoon 3 launched with a cosmetic shop featuring gear that rotates daily. Unlike many modern games, all cosmetics could be purchased with in-game currency earned through free play, with no premium-only cosmetics.</p><p><strong>2022-2023:</strong> Nintendo maintained their consumer-friendly approach throughout, never introducing time-limited exclusives or premium currency requirements. The cosmetic ecosystem remained completely free-to-access from day one.</p><p><strong>2023-2024:</strong> Special cosmetics were introduced for seasonal events (like Splatfests), but remained purchasable with earned currency and eventually became available in regular rotations. Nintendo's commitment to cosmetic fairness remained consistent.</p><p><strong>2024-2025:</strong> Continued expansion of the cosmetic catalog with seasonal themed gear. No price increases or monetization escalation; the system remains one of gaming's fairest cosmetic models.</p>`,
    controversy_html: `<p>Splatoon 3 has generated virtually no cosmetic monetization controversy, which is remarkable for a modern AAA game. The only minor criticism is that some gear has gameplay implications (ability slots), but these are accessible to all players equally regardless of spending.</p>`,
