    editorial_html: `<p><strong>Splatoon 3 is the gold standard for fair cosmetic monetization.</strong> By making all cosmetics purchasable with free, earnable currency and eliminating time-limited exclusivity, Nintendo proves that profitable games don't require predatory monetization. The fairness score of 9/10 reflects that cosmetics have minor gameplay implications (ability distribution) rather than being purely cosmetic, but the complete accessibility negates any fairness concerns.</p><p>This model should be studied by every modern game developer as proof that cosmetic monetization can be ethical, profitable, and consumer-friendly simultaneously. The lack of FOMO, premium currency requirements, and limited-time exclusivity creates a fundamentally different—and vastly superior—player experience compared to industry standards.</p><p>Splatoon 3 demonstrates that cosmetic fairness isn't expensive to implement; it requires only the commitment to prioritize player experience over manipulative monetization tactics. Every player should recognize this as the baseline for acceptable cosmetic systems.</p>`
