    editorial_html: `<p><strong>Among Us represents the gold standard for cosmetic fairness in modern gaming.</strong> With fairness and value scores of 9/10, Among Us demonstrates that cosmetic monetization can be profitable, player-friendly, and completely free of psychological manipulation simultaneously. The complete absence of cosmetic controversy over six years of operation is remarkable.</p><p>Innersloth proved that games don't need aggressive cosmetic monetization to succeed financially. Among Us thrives by respecting player autonomy: all cosmetics are optional, fairly priced, and never time-limited. The cosmetic system never employs FOMO tactics, doesn't bundle unrelated cosmetics, and remains accessible to players of all spending capabilities.</p><p>Every player should use Among Us as the baseline for evaluating cosmetic fairness. If a game's cosmetic system deviates significantly from Among Us's fair model, players should understand they're accepting cosmetic compromise. Among Us proves cosmetic fairness isn't expensive to implement—it requires only the commitment to prioritize players over aggressive monetization.</p>`
