    overview_html: `<p><strong>Candy Crush Saga</strong> represents one of gaming's most predatory monetization models, masquerading as a cosmetic-focused game. While categorized as a cosmetic shop, the actual monetization centers on gameplay-affecting mechanics: lives systems, power-ups, and pay-to-skip progression locks. This blurs cosmetics with core progression systems, creating maximum monetization pressure through psychological design.</p><p>King's flagship title employs sophisticated behavioral psychology: artificial difficulty spikes, strategic lives expiration timing, and power-up bundling designed to maximize spending. The cosmetic framing obscures that players are actually paying for access to core gameplay progression.</p>`,
