    editorial_html: `<p>Minecraft Bedrock's Marketplace represents a reasonable middle ground for cosmetic monetization. While cosmetic prices are higher than Java Edition, the inclusion of UGC and creator revenue sharing creates genuine added value absent in purely corporate cosmetic shops. Supporting independent creators through cosmetic purchases provides direct player-to-developer financial support.</p><p>The fairness score of 7/10 reflects that while cosmetic monetization exists, free cosmetic alternatives, earnable currency options, and creator support systems justify the pricing to a degree. The Bedrock approach acknowledges that cosmetic monetization is acceptable when structured to benefit creators and provide genuine alternatives.</p><p>Players should approach Minecraft Bedrock cosmetics with understanding of the creator-support model. While cosmetics cost more than Java Edition, they directly support independent developers. For players valuing cosmetic fairness above all, Java Edition remains the free cosmetic alternative.</p>`
